{"id":"beeacf2c76d5d297","group":"58","path":"58/batch18/58-df-easton-product.md","title":"Easton-Support Product","display":"df-easton-product — Easton-Support Product","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-easton-product","aliases":["58-df-easton-product"],"display":"df-easton-product — Easton-Support Product","depends_on":["[[../batch02/58-df-poset.md]]","[[../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-easton-product"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-easton-product</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-easton-product — Easton-Support Product"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-poset.md\">../batch02/58-df-poset.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md\">../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"df-easton-product-—-Easton-Product\">df-easton-product — Easton Product</h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec 1,E,\\leq_E\\in V\">\\(I,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec 1,E,\\leq_E\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S\\subseteq V\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"0fbfc19800246e77\" href=\"?note=0fbfc19800246e77\" title=\"../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md\">../batch13/58-df-regular-cardinal.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\subseteq V^3\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Poset}\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{Poset}\\subseteq V^2\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"d3f859dbdd37f018\" href=\"?note=d3f859dbdd37f018\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-poset.md\">../batch02/58-df-poset.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S\\subseteq V^6\">\\(\\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S\\subseteq V^6\\)</span> (本文件定义的 Easton 支持积谓词)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}easton\\text{-}product} \\vdash \\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S(E,\\leq_E,I,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec1)\\leftrightarrow I\\in V\\land\\bigl(\\forall\\kappa\\in I\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\bigr)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\vec P,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec P))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\vec\\leq,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec\\leq))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\vec1,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec1))\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in I\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Poset}(\\vec P(\\kappa),\\vec\\leq(\\kappa))\\land\\vec1(\\kappa)\\in\\vec P(\\kappa)\\land\\forall q\\in\\vec P(\\kappa)\\;(\\langle q,\\vec1(\\kappa)\\rangle\\in\\vec\\leq(\\kappa))\\Bigr)\\land E=\\left\\{p\\in V:\\mathrm{Function}\\left(p,I,\\bigcup\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec P)\\right)\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in I\\;(p(\\kappa)\\in\\vec P(\\kappa))\\land\\forall\\theta\\in V\\;\\left(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\theta)\\to\\left|\\{\\kappa\\in I\\cap\\theta:p(\\kappa)\\neq\\vec1(\\kappa)\\}\\right|&lt;\\theta\\right)\\right\\}\\land\\leq_E=\\left\\{\\langle p,q\\rangle\\in E^2:\\forall\\kappa\\in I\\;(\\langle p(\\kappa),q(\\kappa)\\rangle\\in\\vec\\leq(\\kappa))\\right\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}easton\\text{-}product} \\vdash \\mathrm{EastonProduct}_S(E,\\leq_E,I,\\vec P,\\vec\\leq,\\vec1)\\leftrightarrow I\\in V\\land\\bigl(\\forall\\kappa\\in I\\;\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\kappa)\\bigr)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\vec P,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec P))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\vec\\leq,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec\\leq))\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\vec1,I,\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec1))\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in I\\;\\Bigl(\\mathrm{Poset}(\\vec P(\\kappa),\\vec\\leq(\\kappa))\\land\\vec1(\\kappa)\\in\\vec P(\\kappa)\\land\\forall q\\in\\vec P(\\kappa)\\;(\\langle q,\\vec1(\\kappa)\\rangle\\in\\vec\\leq(\\kappa))\\Bigr)\\land E=\\left\\{p\\in V:\\mathrm{Function}\\left(p,I,\\bigcup\\operatorname{ran}(\\vec P)\\right)\\land\\forall\\kappa\\in I\\;(p(\\kappa)\\in\\vec P(\\kappa))\\land\\forall\\theta\\in V\\;\\left(\\mathrm{RegularCardinal}_S(\\theta)\\to\\left|\\{\\kappa\\in I\\cap\\theta:p(\\kappa)\\neq\\vec1(\\kappa)\\}\\right|&lt;\\theta\\right)\\right\\}\\land\\leq_E=\\left\\{\\langle p,q\\rangle\\in E^2:\\forall\\kappa\\in I\\;(\\langle p(\\kappa),q(\\kappa)\\rangle\\in\\vec\\leq(\\kappa))\\right\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Easton 支持要求每个正则 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta\">\\(\\theta\\)</span> 以下的非顶元坐标少于 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\theta\">\\(\\theta\\)</span>；偏序为逐坐标序。</li>\n<li>适当坐标迫使和额外闭性/链条件可用来控制正则基数处的连续统函数并保持共尾数；这些不是任意 Easton 支持积自动具有的结论。</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"df-easton-product-—-Easton-Product","text":"df-easton-product — Easton Product","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":